#
# spectre forwards a controller raw through its hidraw node
# (docs/design/audio-cursor-gamepad.md#raw-controllers), which udev
# leaves to root unless something tags it; Steam's own rules would, but
# the image has no Steam. This gives the signed-in kiosk user (uaccess:
# whoever is active on seat0) the hidraw nodes of the controller vendors
# whose pads have host drivers worth reaching: Sony, Nintendo, Valve,
# Microsoft (Xbox pads over Bluetooth) and 8BitDo. Anything else is
# forwarded as a standard pad.
#
# Matched on the HID device's name, bus:vendor:product.N, so USB and
# Bluetooth alike. Before 73-seat-late, which applies uaccess.
KERNEL=="hidraw*", KERNELS=="*:054C:*|*:057E:*|*:28DE:*|*:045E:*|*:2DC8:*", TAG+="uaccess"
